# Target: .github/CODEOWNERS
#
# The catch-all is the only line every repo shares, and it is the one that makes
# every other rule reviewable: without an owner on the whole tree, a PR can
# change a gate's own configuration with nobody required to look.
#
# A repo adds a line per escape hatch it actually has — `.standardsignore`,
# `.standards.mode`, `.docs-lint.mode`, `tools/floors.tsv`. Those are not in the
# shared set because a rule naming a path the repo does not have reads as
# coverage while matching nothing, and CODEOWNERS gives no warning for it.
